{"count":1088,"next":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=10&page_size=100","previous":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=8&page_size=100","results":[{"id":1013,"title":"AFP achieves enhanced capabilities in AJEX DAGITPA 2022","slug":"afp-achieves-enhanced-capabilities-in-ajex-dagitpa-2022","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/AJC1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"572\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/AJC1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) has achieved its targets in enhancing interoperability and readiness in joint operations as it ends this year’s AFP Joint Exercise DAGITPA (Dagat, Langit, Lupa) on Friday, November 18.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP Chief of Staff, Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente Bacarro who represented Department of National Defense Senior Undersecretary Jose Faustino Jr. presided over the closing ceremony held at Camp Aguinaldo.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/AJC1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-18T14:34:55+08:00","hits":380},{"id":1014,"title":"CHANGE OF CHIEF OF OFFICE ","slug":"change-of-chief-of-office-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/PAL3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"624\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/PAL3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Office for Strategic Studies and Strategy Management (OSSSM) welcomes its new chief on Monday, November 14, in a joint Change of Chief of Office and Retirement Ceremony presided by The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP VAdm Rommel Anthony SD Reyes at the General Headquarters, AFP.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">BGen Edgardo C Palma relinquished his post as Chief, OSSSM to Col Haroun-al Rashid I Jaji after reaching the mandatory retirement age of 56 and over 35 years of outstanding military service.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/PAL3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-16T14:43:35+08:00","hits":1701},{"id":1015,"title":"AFP holds Live Fire drill in Palawan","slug":"afp-holds-live-fire-drill-in-palawan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/CAL5.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"448\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/CAL5.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) conducted the Combined Arms and Littoral Live Fire Exercise (CALLFEX) demonstration as part of the AFP Joint Exercise (AJEX) “DAGIT-PA” on November 15, 2022 at Punta Baja, Rizal, Palawan.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The CALLFEX seeks to enhance the interoperability of Army forces with other branches of service in Joint and Combined Arms operations. It aims to improve the synchronization and integration of available assets, especially in providing support to ground forces to defeat the enemy.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/CAL5.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-16T14:41:01+08:00","hits":300},{"id":1016,"title":"AFP JOINS KADIWA NG PASKO LAUNCHING","slug":"afp-joins-kadiwa-ng-pasko-launching","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/KAD7.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/KAD7.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines joins the nationwide launching of the Kadiwa ng Pasko at the Wellness Center inside Camp Aguinaldo in Quezon City on Wednesday, November 16.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Kadiwa ng Pasko project is an initiative of the national government led by the Department of Agriculture aimed at providing a market to the country’s local agricultural producers while at the same time giving the public access to affordable and high-quality products during this yuletide season.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/KAD7.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-16T14:37:20+08:00","hits":220},{"id":1017,"title":"VISCOM Change of Command and Retirement Ceremony","slug":"viscom-change-of-command-and-retirement-ceremony","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/0-02-06-d93389c8bd533363992db3921ea14b148540b6da07ce7fcbfd47dcbdc0f0b582_e42e500e6c15d42c.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"553\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/0-02-06-d93389c8bd533363992db3921ea14b148540b6da07ce7fcbfd47dcbdc0f0b582_e42e500e6c15d42c.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CHANGE OF COMMAND | AFP Chief of Staff LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro presided over the Change of Command and Retirement Ceremony for LtGen Robert Dauz, the Commander of Visayas Command who bowed out of the military on Monday, November 14.</p>\r\n<p>LtGen Dauz served in the Armed Forces of the Philippines for over 38 years of outstanding military career. A member of the Philippine Military Academy “Maringal” Class of 1988, he rose through the ranks from being a Platoon Leader and Company Commander in the 1st Light Armor Battalion. He was also designated in key staff and command positions including as Vice Commander of the Philippine Army and commander of the Armor Division.</p>\r\n<p>LtGen Dauz relinquished his post as Commander of Visayas Command to MGen Benedict Arevalo, the current commander of the 3rd Infantry Division, who will now oversee joint military operations in the Visayas in an acting capacity. (Photos by A2C Castro/PAO, AFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/0-02-06-d93389c8bd533363992db3921ea14b148540b6da07ce7fcbfd47dcbdc0f0b582_e42e500e6c15d42c.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-15T14:47:12+08:00","hits":214},{"id":1018,"title":"ARRIVAL HONORS","slug":"arrival-honors-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/VVM1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/VVM1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP) LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro welcomes President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. upon the President's arrival on Monday, November 14 from his participation in the ASEAN Summit in Cambodia.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The CSAFP was joined by Philippine Air Force Commanding General LtGen Connor Anthony Canlas Sr, Philippine Navy Acting Flag Officer-In Command RAdm Caesar Bernard Valencia, and Philippine Army Vice Commander MGen Adonis Bajao. PNP Chief Gen Rodolfo Azurin and PCG Commandant Adm Artemio Abu were also in attendance.///</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photo by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAO, AFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/VVM1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-14T14:59:13+08:00","hits":255},{"id":1019,"title":"US VETERANS DAY","slug":"us-veterans-day","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/5776086A-C6B1-41F6-B405-158E65E772D5.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/5776086A-C6B1-41F6-B405-158E65E772D5.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro joined the commemoration of US Veterans Day at the Manila American Cemetery and Memorial in Fort Bonifacio. US Ambassador to the Philippines, Honorable MaryKay Carlson led the ceremony on 11 November 2022 honoring the service and sacrifice of US and Filipino veterans.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/5776086A-C6B1-41F6-B405-158E65E772D5.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-11T15:04:15+08:00","hits":248},{"id":1020,"title":"Philippine Air Force's Super Tucanos, Black Hawk Arrive in Palawan for AJEX DAGITPA 2022","slug":"philippine-air-forces-super-tucanos-black-hawk-arrive-in-palawan-for-ajex-dagitpa-2022","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/315232974_486551740173908_1683588986188991065_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/315232974_486551740173908_1683588986188991065_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Two A-29 Super Tucanos with tail numbers 1902 and 1905, and a Black Hawk with tail Number 106 arrived on November 9-10 in Antonio Bautista Air Base as Philippine Air Force's commitment to the ongoing AFP Joint Exercise DAGITPA 2022 in Western Command's Joint Operations Area.<br /><br />\"We welcome with pride our Philippine Air Force pilots, crew, and modern fleet of aircraft here in the Western Frontier,\" Vice Admiral Alberto B Carlos PN, the Commander WESCOM said.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/315232974_486551740173908_1683588986188991065_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-11T07:04:41+08:00","hits":199},{"id":1021,"title":"BRP Bacolod (LS550), Philippine Army Participants of AJEX DAGITPA 2022 Arrive in Palawan","slug":"brp-bacolod-ls550-philippine-army-participants-of-ajex-dagitpa-2022-arrive-in-palawan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/AJEX1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"449\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/AJEX1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The Philippine Navy vessel BRP Bacolod City (LS550) arrived yesterday, 09 November 2022 at the the 2Lt Lagare Pier in Puerto Princesa City, together with the personnel and assets of 3rd Infantry Division and 15th Infantry Battalion of the Philippine Army who are participating in the AFP Joint Exercise DAGITPA 2022.</p>\r\n<p>\"Western Command cordially welcomes our gallant Army comrades to the Western Frontier all the way from Roxas City, Capiz,\" said Vice Admiral Alberto B Carlos PN, the Commander of Western Command.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/AJEX1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-10T15:10:41+08:00","hits":231},{"id":1022,"title":"4th Quarter NSED","slug":"4th-quarter-nsed","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/NSED7.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/NSED7.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines participated in the fourth quarter nationwide simultaneous Earthquake Drill on Thursday, November 10. Units and offices within military camps and installations joined the drill spearheaded by the Office of Civil Defense which also highlighted the call for tsunami awareness and preparedness as part of the World Tsunami Awareness observance.///</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photos from AFP Peace and Development Office, 11th CMO Battalion, and AFP Reserve Command)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/NSED7.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-10T15:08:56+08:00","hits":262},{"id":1023,"title":"NOLCOM dismantles 3 CPP-NPA Guerrilla Fronts","slug":"nolcom-dismantles-3-cpp-npa-guerrilla-fronts","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/NOL6.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/NOL6.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines' Northern Luzon Command (NOLCOM) based in Tarlac City has dismantled three guerrilla fronts of the CPP-NPA as of 4th quarter 2022 under the leadership of Lieutenant General Ernesto Torres Jr.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">NOLCOM’s intensified operations led to the reduction of CPP-NPA’s manpower and firearms with 417 communist terrorists and supporters neutralized, and 163 firearms seized.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/NOL6.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-09T15:12:10+08:00","hits":283},{"id":1024,"title":"Gender Mainstreaming","slug":"gender-mainstreaming","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/GAD3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/GAD3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Acting Vice Chief of Staff LtGen William Gonzales and Atty Kristine Rosary Yuzon-Chavez, Executive Director of the Philippine Commission on Women, renewed a partnership agreement centered on mainstreaming gender and development matters in the military on Monday, November 7, at the AFP General Headquarters in Quezon City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/GAD3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-08T15:15:18+08:00","hits":683},{"id":1025,"title":"Building Partnership","slug":"building-partnership","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/VIE1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"622\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/VIE1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro met with Senior Lieutenant General Nguyen Tan Cuong, Chief of General Staff of Vietnam People's Army and Vice Minister of National Defense of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam on Monday, November 7, at the General Headquarters in Quezon City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/VIE1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-08T15:13:43+08:00","hits":263},{"id":1026,"title":"AFP Joint Exercise “DAGIT-PA” opens","slug":"afp-joint-exercise-dagit-pa-opens","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/AJEX5.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/AJEX5.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) officially opened the AFP Joint Exercise (AJEX) “DAGIT-PA” on Monday, November 7, in a ceremony presided by the AFP Chief of Staff, Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente Bacarro at the General Headquarters canopy area.<br /><br />DAGIT-PA, which stands for “Dagat-Langit-Lupa” is an AFP-wide/AFP-only exercise that integrates Philippine Navy, Philippine Air Force, Philippine Army, and AFP Special Operations Forces to level up capabilities to accomplish missions in the sea, air, and land.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/AJEX5.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-07T15:22:43+08:00","hits":1068},{"id":1027,"title":"Philippine Marines Anniversary","slug":"philippine-marines-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/PMC3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/PMC3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff LtGen Bartolome Vicente Bacarro led the wreath-laying ceremony at the Marine Heroes Monument, Marine Barracks Rudiardo Brown, Fort Bonifacio, Taguig City on Monday, November 7, as part of the 72nd birthday of the Philippine Marine Corps (PMC).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With the theme, “TEAM MARINES @ 72: Katuwang ng bawat Pilipino tungo sa mas mapayapa, maunlad, at nagkakaisang bansa,” the PMC will highlight \"illustrious past and honor the distinguished legacy that the Marine forefathers have built in the last seven decades.\"</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/PMC3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-07T15:19:22+08:00","hits":316},{"id":1028,"title":"AFP Statement on the Status of Communist Insurgency","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-status-of-communist-insurgency","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The CPP/NPA/NDF is losing not just in tactical battles, but in relevance as well. With the remaining 24 guerilla fronts, 19 of which are weakened and inactive, this leaves the Communist Party with five (5) fronts to pursue its violent means of achieving political objectives. With the relentless efforts of the government security forces to subdue insurgency, the CPP found its lower politico-military organs on the run, therefore incapable of implementing party programs, the lifeblood of its existence.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-06T15:25:18+08:00","hits":335},{"id":1029,"title":"Communist NPA terrorists commit new human rights, IHL violations in murder of CAFGU, civilians","slug":"communist-npa-terrorists-commit-new-human-rights-ihl-violations-in-murder-of-cafgu-civilians","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div dir=\"auto\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City </strong>-<strong> </strong>The communist NPA terrorists (CNTs) added another atrocity to their long list of Human Rights and International Humanitarian Law (HR/IHL) violations upon the discovery of the remains of five individuals who were executed by their members.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The AFP earlier condemned the execution of two (2) CAFGU members and three (3) civilians whose bodies were found in shallow graves on October 30 in Santiago, Agusan Del Norte.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The efforts of the AFP alongside the local police of Santiago led to the successful exhumation of the bodies of said individuals who were earlier abducted and then murdered by the CNTs. ","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-05T15:27:27+08:00","hits":291},{"id":1030,"title":"AFP receives three vehicles, office equipment","slug":"afp-receives-three-vehicles-office-equipment","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/0-02-06-f0e290f9b39e3ec3839798f90e41410ba25a47e932e078cdbe6de6389b41c014_bebf1bfbcef7a2c4.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"547\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/0-02-06-f0e290f9b39e3ec3839798f90e41410ba25a47e932e078cdbe6de6389b41c014_bebf1bfbcef7a2c4.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>DONATION CEREMONY | The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP VAdm  Rommel Anthony SD Reyes received three Toyota Hi-Ace Commuter Vans and other office equipment from the AFP Mutual Benefit Association Incorporated (MBAI) as part of the latter’s corporate social responsibility program. The donations were handed over in a ceremony on November 3, at the General Headquarters in Quezon City. The AFP Civil Relations Service, Office of Legislative Affairs, and AFP Education, Training, and Doctrine Command each received one vehicle, while the Office of the Special Service and the Office for Strategic Studies and Strategic Management received computer sets and office equipment. (Photos by Sgt Manzano/PAO, AFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/0-02-06-f0e290f9b39e3ec3839798f90e41410ba25a47e932e078cdbe6de6389b41c014_bebf1bfbcef7a2c4.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-04T15:32:58+08:00","hits":236},{"id":1031,"title":"AFP Statement on the Exhumed Remains of 5 Persons in Agusan del Norte","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-exhumed-remains-of-5-persons-in-agusan-del-norte","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP condoles with the families of the CAFGU members and innocent civilians who were summarily executed by suspected NPA members in Northeastern Mindanao. The remains of five persons who were reported to be abducted by NPA members were finally exhumed on Sunday morning, October 30, 2022, at Sitio Baraboto, Brgy Curva, Santiago, Agusan del Norte. We hope that the recovery of the victims’ remains will help their families as they continue to seek closure and justice. We also pray that the victims will find eternal peace now that they will be placed in their final resting place.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-11-03T15:34:35+08:00","hits":185},{"id":1032,"title":"Joint Change of Chiefs of Office","slug":"joint-change-of-chiefs-of-office","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/COCOO4.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/COCOO4.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) held a Joint Change of Chief of Office Ceremony for three key offices on Thursday, October 27 in Camp Aguinaldo with the Deputy Chief of Staff and concurrent Acting Vice Chief of Staff, Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes PN as the presiding officer.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Brigadier General Jose Maria R Cuerpo PA assumed as the new Deputy Chief of Staff for Personnel, J1 replacing Brigadier General Rommel P Roldan PAF who led the office in an acting capacity.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/COCOO4.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-28T15:41:34+08:00","hits":556},{"id":1033,"title":"AFP installs new Commander of Civil Relations Service","slug":"afp-installs-new-commander-of-civil-relations-service","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The AFP installed BGen Arvin R Lagamon PA as the new Commander of the Civil Relations Service, AFP (CRSAFP) replacing the Acting Commander, Col Medel M Aguilar, in a ceremony held on Wednesday, October 26 in Camp Aguinaldo.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The CRSAFP is the primary unit of the AFP that engages the general public through information support activities and community relation programs. The unit also conducts stakeholder engagement with other government agencies and non-government organizations in providing public service to needy communities.</p>\r\n","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-28T15:36:54+08:00","hits":4237},{"id":1034,"title":"AFP inaugurates new TIKAS Projects in General Headquarters","slug":"afp-inaugurates-new-tikas-projects-in-general-headquarters","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/TIKAS1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/TIKAS1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - AFP Chief of Staff Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente Bacarro led the inauguration and blessing ceremony of the newly-completed TIKAS Projects inside the General Headquarters on Tuesday, October 25.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The TIKAS or \"Tatag ng Imprastraktura para sa Kapayapaan at Seguridad\" program is part of the concerted efforts of the Department of National Defense (DND) and the Department of Public Works and Highways (DPWH) to shore up the defense and security capabilities of the AFP.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/TIKAS1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-26T15:47:26+08:00","hits":381},{"id":1035,"title":"CEISSAFP Change of Command","slug":"ceissafp-change-of-command","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/CEI3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"656\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/CEI3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) installs Navy Captain Marcos Y Imperio PN(GSC) as the new Commander of the Communications, Electronics and Information Systems Services, AFP (CEISSAFP) on Tuesday, October 25 at the CEISSAFP headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City with the AFP Deputy Chief of Staff and concurrent Acting Vice Chief of Staff, Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes as the presiding officer.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Captain Imperio replaced Colonel Joselito T Lopena PAF(GSC), who commanded the CEISSAFP in an acting capacity since August 2022.<br /><br />(Photos by Sgt Joymar Niño Dave Soria PAF/PAOAFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/CEI3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-26T15:45:22+08:00","hits":1732},{"id":1036,"title":"AFP-PNP-PCG Olympics ends, Team Army declared champion","slug":"afp-pnp-pcg-olympics-ends-team-army-declared-champion","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/OLY6.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/OLY6.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), Philippine National Police (PNP), and Philippine Coast Guard (PCG) closed its annual inter-service sporting event on Tuesday, October 25 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand in Camp Aguinaldo with the AFP Chief of Staff, Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente Bacarro PA as presiding officer, and Chairman Jose Emmanuel Eala of the Philippine Sports Commission as special guest.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">\"This event symbolized the solidarity and comradeship among the men and women of our defense, law enforcement, and security sectors. It is vital that the AFP, PNP, and PCG continue to foster robust partnerships to sustain cohesive and concerted efforts in addressing the complexities of our security environment,\" Lt. Gen. Bacarro said.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/OLY6.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-26T15:43:27+08:00","hits":429},{"id":1037,"title":"Col Musñgi assumes as new JTF-NCR commander","slug":"col-musngi-assumes-as-new-jtf-ncr-commander","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/F313D503-85FA-43FB-9153-22AE03817B09.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/F313D503-85FA-43FB-9153-22AE03817B09.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines installed Colonel Alexei Musñgi as the new commander of Joint Task Force-National Capital Region (JTF-NCR). AFP Chief of Staff Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente Bacarro presided over the Change of Command Ceremony on Monday, October 24, at the AFP Commissioned Officers Club in Camp Aguinaldo.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Colonel Musñgi previously served as the commander of the 1002nd Infantry Brigade. He was also the Assistant Chief of Staff for Operations, G3, Philippine Army, and commander of the 48th Infantry Battalion.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/F313D503-85FA-43FB-9153-22AE03817B09.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-24T15:49:19+08:00","hits":1042},{"id":1038,"title":"BGen Licudine PA assumes as new AFPETDC Commander","slug":"bgen-licudine-pa-assumes-as-new-afpetdc-commander","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p>CHANGE OF COMMAND | Major General Charlton Sean M Gaerlan PN(M) relinquished his post as the Commander of the Armed Forces of the Philippines Education, Training, and Doctrine Command to Brigadier General Marvin L Licudine PA in a Change of Command Ceremony held Thursday, October 20.</p>\r\n<p>Earlier in August, MGen Gaerlan was appointed as the Commandant of the Philippine Marine Corps. On the other hand, BGen Licudine comes in from his stint as Chief of the AFP Peace and Development Office. Prior to this, he served as the Chief of the Office of the Army Adjutant. He is a member of the Philippine Military Academy Makatao Class of 1989 and holds a Master in Business Administration and Masters in Management.</p>\r\n<p>The Acting Vice Chief of Staff VAdm Rommel Anthony SD Reyes PN presided over the ceremony held at the Manipula Hall in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. (Photos by A2C Castro/PAO, AFP)</p>","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-21T15:51:07+08:00","hits":2374},{"id":1039,"title":"AFP units deliver aid to typhoon-hit residents in Northern Luzon","slug":"afp-units-deliver-aid-to-typhoon-hit-residents-in-northern-luzon","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/HADR1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/HADR1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) together with other government agencies joined the local Social Welfare Development Office in distributing relief goods and assisting residents affected by Typhoon Neneng and Tropical Storm Maymay that hit Northern Luzon last week.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A total of 370 DSWD food packs were distributed by the Philippine Army's 77th Infantry Battalion and other government agencies to the typhoon-affected families in Barangay Alba, San Miguel, and Taytay Baggao, Cagayan on October 16, 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/HADR1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-17T16:37:55+08:00","hits":201},{"id":1040,"title":"AFP Statement on the 5th Year Anniversary of Marawi Liberation","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-5th-year-anniversary-of-marawi-liberation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines shares the honor and glory of saluting all our heroes who helped liberate the City of Marawi from the clutches of terrorism, five years ago. Their service and sacrifice serve as a legacy that will live on forever in the hearts and minds of the Filipino people.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">We owe it to the valiant and courageous men and women in uniform who fought the Maute terrorist group so that we could still fly freely the Philippine Flag over Marawi City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-17T15:56:17+08:00","hits":199},{"id":1041,"title":"No Soldier's Orphan Left Behind: 5,000 graduates, 3,000 grantees assisted by AFPEBS as of 2022","slug":"no-soldiers-orphan-left-behind-5-000-graduates-3-000-grantees-assisted-by-afpebs-as-of-2022","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/EBSO23.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"671\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/EBSO23.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With the new school year kicking off, the AFP Educational Benefit System (AFPEBS) reported an estimated total of 5,000 graduates from S.Y. 2000-2021 and more than 3,000 continuing grantees for 2022, who are mostly dependents of killed-in-action military personnel.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Several AFPEBSO grantees nationwide completed their education and are now pursuing careers in different fields. Some grantees also opted to join military service to follow in the footsteps of their loved ones who gave their lives protecting the peace and stability of the country.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/EBSO23.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-14T16:44:37+08:00","hits":379},{"id":1042,"title":"AFP Statement on the Declaration of the Davao Region as Insurgency-free","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-declaration-of-the-davao-region-as-insurgency-free","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November 2022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/November 2022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines lauds the troops of Eastern Mindanao Command and the 10th Infantry Division for a job well done that resulted in the declaration of the whole Davao region as insurgency-free.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The joint resolution signed by the Regional Peace and Order Council composed of Local Chief Executives from various Local Government Units (LGUs) of Region 11 signifies the success of the Whole of Nation approach in ending the insurgency in the area.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/November%202022/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-14T16:41:28+08:00","hits":244},{"id":1043,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff commends Diamond Troopers","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-commends-diamond-troopers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/DIA2.jpg\" width=\"854\" height=\"569\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/DIA2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) visited the valiant troops of the Joint Task Force Diamond dubbed as the ‘Diamond Troopers’ in Cagayan De Oro City, Wednesday.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente Bacarro commended the men and women of the Joint Task Force Diamond for their exemplary achievements in protecting the peace and catalyzing development in their areas of operation.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/DIA2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-13T16:46:39+08:00","hits":174},{"id":1044,"title":"AFP holds first-ever simultaneous Multilateral Naval Exercises","slug":"afp-holds-first-ever-simultaneous-multilateral-naval-exercises","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/SAM3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/SAM3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) opened the first-ever simultaneous conduct of Maritime Training Activity SAMA-SAMA (MTA SAMA-SAMA) and LUMBAS on Tuesday, October 11.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Chief of Staff of the AFP, Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente Bacarro presided over the opening ceremony at the Naval Forces Central (NAVFORCEN) in Lapu-Lapu City, Cebu.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/SAM3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-12T16:50:46+08:00","hits":204},{"id":1045,"title":"On Preparations for TD MAYMAY","slug":"on-preparations-for-td-maymay","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>The Armed Forces of the Philippines through the Northern Luzon Command (NOLCOM) led by Lt. Gen. Ernesto Torres Jr has already alerted all units in Northern Luzon for possible deployment in areas expected to be affected by Tropical Depression Maymay. These include the disaster response units of all battalions and brigades under NOLCOM's joint operational area that will be affected by the storm. Air and naval assets under operational control of NOLCOM are also on standby and may be used for aerial assessment, transport, and evacuation operations.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-12T16:48:55+08:00","hits":211},{"id":1046,"title":"Death of NPA spokesman, a big blow to CTG in Central Visayas","slug":"death-of-npa-spokesman-a-big-blow-to-ctg-in-central-visayas","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Romeo Nanta who used the nom de guerre Juanito Magbanua was killed in an encounter in Brgy. Carabalan, Himamaylan City, Negros Occidental on October 10, 2022. His death is a big blow to the CPP/NPA/NDF.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Nanta is the spokesperson of the Communist Terrorist Group's Apolinario Gatmaitan Command and Commanding Officer of the Regional Operational Command of the NPA units operating in Negros Island and the entire Central Visayas region. He is directly responsible for all the crimes committed by NPA members under his command. He has existing warrants of arrest for rebellion, robbery-in-band, and attempted and frustrated murder.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-10T16:52:37+08:00","hits":213},{"id":1047,"title":"Meeting at the U.S. Indo-Pacific Command Headquarters, Honolulu, Hawaii","slug":"meeting-at-the-u-s-indo-pacific-command-headquarters-honolulu-hawaii","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/E3D62CE1-FA90-497A-9F2D-8A126453C4B5.png\" width=\"497\" height=\"356\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/E3D62CE1-FA90-497A-9F2D-8A126453C4B5.png\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">LTGEN BARTOLOME VICENTE O BACARRO PA, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines and ADMIRAL JOHN C AQUILINO, Commander of the U.S. Indo-Pacific Command co-chaired the 2022 Mutual Defense Board and Security Engagement Board (MDB-SEB)on 27 September 2022.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Mutual Defense Board and Security Engagement Board was created to tackle traditional and non-traditional security concerns faced by both the Philippines and the United States as partners. It is composed of key leaders from the Armed Forces of the Philippines, Philippine National Police, Philippine Coast Guard, Department of National Defense, and the Department of Foreign Affairs.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/E3D62CE1-FA90-497A-9F2D-8A126453C4B5.png","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-08T16:59:47+08:00","hits":255},{"id":1048,"title":"AFP highlights accomplishments for PBBM’s 1st 100 days","slug":"afp-highlights-accomplishments-for-pbbm-s-1st-100-days","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines highlights its accomplishments in its various campaigns and ongoing programs that contributed to President Ferdinand Marcos Jr’s first 100 days in office.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">These accomplishments include gains in internal peace and security operations, external defense, modernization and capability development, and international bilateral and multi-lateral engagements.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/MEDIA_RELEASE_CARD.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-08T16:56:06+08:00","hits":283},{"id":1049,"title":"AFP forms fact-finding committee for missing labor activists","slug":"afp-forms-fact-finding-committee-for-missing-labor-activists","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The AFP created a fact-finding committee that will “conduct speedy, comprehensive, and exhaustive investigation” on the continued disappearance of labor activists Elizabeth Magbanua and Alipio Juat.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This was done through a letter directive dated October 5, 2022, which is one of the AFP’s actions in compliance with the Petition for Writ of Amparo filed by the relatives of the missing persons before the Supreme Court and granted by the Court of Appeals in a decision on September 9.</p>\r\n","featured_image":null,"image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-08T14:30:56+08:00","hits":653},{"id":1050,"title":"AFP submits thousands of CTG human rights abuses to CHR","slug":"afp-submits-thousands-of-ctg-human-rights-abuses-to-chr","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/CLOAC2.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"456\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/CLOAC2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City— The Director of the Armed Forces of the Philippines Center for Law of Armed Conflict (AFPCLOAC), BGEN JOEL ALEJANDRO S NACNAC PA submitted on October 6 (Thursday) thousands of recorded Communist Terrorist Group's (CTG's) human rights abuses to the Commission on Human Rights (CHR).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Chairperson Hon. Richard P Palpal-Latoc received the list of 2,443 Communist Terrorist Group (CTG) Human Rights (HR) abuses from CYs 1968 to 2009, and resubmitted HR/IHL CTG violations covering 2010 to 1st Semester 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/CLOAC2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-06T17:02:45+08:00","hits":535},{"id":1051,"title":"AFP, DND turnover lots to Cebu Government ","slug":"afp-dnd-turnover-lots-to-cebu-government","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/CEB4.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/CEB4.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the Department of National Defense (DND) turned over 16 parcels of lands back to the Cebu Provincial Government in a ceremony held Monday, October 3.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP Chief of Staff, Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente Bacarro and DND Senior Undersecretary and Officer-in-Charge Jose Faustino Jr graced the event at the Capitol Social Hall in Cebu City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/CEB4.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-04T17:11:16+08:00","hits":333},{"id":1052,"title":"AFP, humanitarian group formalize cooperation","slug":"afp-humanitarian-group-formalize-cooperation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/HUM1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/HUM1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP Aguinaldo, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the Mindanao Humanitarian Volunteers for Peace Inc., (MHVP) formalized through a Memorandum of Agreement an ongoing partnership that delivers services in remote and conflict-affected communities in the country.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The agreement was signed on Monday, October 3, at the AFP General Headquarters by The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP VAdm Rommel Anthony SD Reyes on behalf of the AFP Chief of Staff, and MHVP President Dr. Maria Theresa Heyrosa.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/HUM1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-10-04T17:04:58+08:00","hits":256},{"id":1053,"title":"OPAPRU, AFP highlight gains, future plans on peace process","slug":"opapru-afp-highlight-gains-future-plans-on-peace-process","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/OPAP1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"505\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/OPAP1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Office of the Presidential Adviser on Peace, Reconciliation, and Unity (OPAPRU) and Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) highlighted the significant developments on various peace tables during the OPAPRU-AFP Peace Symposium held Thursday, September 29 in Camp Aguinaldo.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Among those discussed are the government's peace accords with the Moro Islamic Liberation Front (MILF), Moro National Liberation Front (MNLF), Cordillera Peoples Liberation Army (CPLA), and other peace-inclined groups including ending the local communist armed conflict in the country.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/OPAP1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-30T20:11:57+08:00","hits":415},{"id":1054,"title":"AFP concludes 51st Pacific Area Senior Officers Logistics Seminar","slug":"afp-concludes-51st-pacific-area-senior-officers-logistics-seminar","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/PAS1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/PAS1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The 51st iteration of the Pacific Area Senior Officers Logistics Seminar (PASOLS) hosted by the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) in Manila was concluded on Thursday, September 29.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The six-day activity held at the Conrad Manila in Pasay City resulted to productive discussions on overcoming common logistics problems and developing mutually beneficial solution among the participants.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/PAS1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-30T17:25:37+08:00","hits":243},{"id":1055,"title":"AFP-PNP-PCG opens first face-to-face Olympics since pandemic","slug":"afp-pnp-pcg-opens-first-face-to-face-olympics-since-pandemic","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October 2023/2DFBF786-7374-44A1-AE4B-3345311DB781.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/October 2023/2DFBF786-7374-44A1-AE4B-3345311DB781.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), Philippine National Police (PNP), and Philippine Coast Guard (PCG) opened the face-to-face annual inter-service sporting event on Friday, September 30 after it was postponed due to the COVID19 pandemic.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Athletes from the AFP, PNP, and PCG gathered at the 2022 AFP-PNP-PCG Olympics opening ceremony held at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand in Camp Aguinaldo.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/October%202023/2DFBF786-7374-44A1-AE4B-3345311DB781.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-30T17:15:14+08:00","hits":528},{"id":1056,"title":"Building Partnership Against Terrorism","slug":"building-partnership-against-terrorism","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/viber_image_2022-09-29_09-34-26-338.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"519\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/viber_image_2022-09-29_09-34-26-338.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - AFP Acting Vice Chief of Staff (VCSAFP) Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes met with His Excellency Roger Noble, Australian Ambassador for Counter Terrorism (CT), during the latter’s courtesy call on 28 September 2022 at the General Headquarters in Quezon City.</p>\r\n<p>In their meeting, Ambassador Noble noted that the Philippines has some of the best practices in countering local terrorism which his government can learn from. VAdm Reyes commented that the support of the government and the people helped the Armed Forces effectively address this concern. The enactment of laws served as basis in dealing with local communist insurgency and terrorism.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/viber_image_2022-09-29_09-34-26-338.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-29T20:15:48+08:00","hits":265},{"id":1057,"title":"AFP continues HADR ops in Karding-hit areas","slug":"afp-continues-hadr-ops-in-karding-hit-areas","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/KD3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"360\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/KD3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Response (HADR) operations by various units of the Armed Forces of the Philippines continue in areas hit by Super Typhoon Karding.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Earlier today, September 27, relief operations were conducted by the 202nd Infantry Brigade to affected families in an evacuation center in Real, Quezon. 1st Infantry Battalion together with the Philippine Coast Guard and other Volunteers loaded more than 1000 boxes of relief goods from DSWD and 900 bottles of drinking water and 100 boxes of sardines from GMA Kapuso Foundation at the Polillo Port in Polillo, Quezon for distribution to affected residents.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/KD3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-27T20:17:03+08:00","hits":271},{"id":1058,"title":"AFP deployed HADR teams to Karding affected areas","slug":"afp-deployed-hadr-teams-to-karding-affected-areas","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines deployed Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Response (HADR) teams to areas affected by Super Typhoon (TS) Karding in North, Central, and Southern Luzon as early as September 25 to help affected residents.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In Northern Luzon, AFP’s Northern Luzon Command utilized its 203rd, Ready Reserve Battalion to support the pre-emptive evacuation conducted by the MDRRMO in four barangays of Aritao, Nueva Viscaya. The Marine Battalion Landing Team 10 also rescued four families near the riverbanks in Brgy. Esteves, Casiguran, Aurora on September 25.</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/26AA8050-B3EC-43FE-9A54-30C8A7AE25AE.jpeg\" width=\"780\" height=\"1040\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/26AA8050-B3EC-43FE-9A54-30C8A7AE25AE.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/26AA8050-B3EC-43FE-9A54-30C8A7AE25AE.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-26T20:22:03+08:00","hits":213},{"id":1059,"title":"AFP hosts 51st Pacific Area Senior Officers Logistics Seminar","slug":"afp-hosts-51st-pacific-area-senior-officers-logistics-seminar","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/FA522C64-50A3-46D8-A9A4-DE210F0E7FA7.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/FA522C64-50A3-46D8-A9A4-DE210F0E7FA7.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines hosts the 51st iteration of the Pacific Area Senior Officers Logistics Seminar (PASOLS) starting today and will end on September 29.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Established in 1971, PASOLS originally started with nine member nations and has since expanded to 31 member nations.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/FA522C64-50A3-46D8-A9A4-DE210F0E7FA7.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-26T20:20:39+08:00","hits":387},{"id":1060,"title":"AFP receives equipment from Olympian Hidilyn Diaz","slug":"afp-receives-equipment-from-olympian-hidilyn-diaz","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/HD5.jpg\" width=\"1600\" height=\"939\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/HD5.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) received weightlifting equipment from Olympic Gold Medalist and Philippine Air Force Staff Sergeant Hidilyn Diaz-Naranjo on Friday, September 23.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The donation was in partnership with the Samahang Weightlifting ng Pilipinas (SWP) headed by its president, Mr Monico Puentevella. It aims to promote weightlifting events among AFP personnel and their dependents with an end view of developing more future world-class soldier-athletes.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/HD5.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-23T20:36:33+08:00","hits":315},{"id":1061,"title":"AFP, Metrobank Foundation recognize 2021 and 2022 Outstanding Filipino Award for Soldiers","slug":"afp-metrobank-foundation-recognize-2021-and-2022-outstanding-filipino-award-for-soldiers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/MB3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/MB3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines and the Metrobank Foundation Inc., (MBFI) recognized six soldiers who were recipients of the 2021 and 2022 Metrobank Foundation Outstanding Filipino Award for Soldiers (MFOFAS) on Thursday, September 22, at the AFP General Headquarters in Quezon City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Acting Vice Chief of Staff AFP VAdm Anthony SD Reyes who represented the AFP Chief of Staff, and MBFI President and Chief Executive Officer Mr Aniceto M Sobrepeña led the honors for the select outstanding military officers and enlisted personnel.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/MB3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-23T20:34:37+08:00","hits":371},{"id":1062,"title":"Looking for: Audio-Visual Aids Technician I","slug":"looking-for-audio-visual-aids-technician-i","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/AA6.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/AA6.jpg\" /></p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/AA6.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-23T20:27:06+08:00","hits":214},{"id":1063,"title":"MILITARY DIPLOMACY","slug":"military-diplomacy","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/DIP1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/DIP1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">His Excellency Shambhu S Kumaran, Ambassador of India to the Philippines receivAed a warm welcome from the Armed Forces of the Philippines during his visit to the General Headquarters in Quezon City on Wednesday, September 21.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ambassador Kumaran and AFP Chief of Staff Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro discussed fostering long-term bilateral military cooperation between the two countries, particularly on education and training. They also affirmed both countries' shared values toward a free and open Indo-Pacific region. ///</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photo by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAO, AFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/DIP1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-22T20:40:11+08:00","hits":308},{"id":1064,"title":"AFP thanks BCDA for support in its modernization","slug":"afp-thanks-bcda-for-support-in-its-modernization","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/viber_image_2022-09-20_09-02-02-380.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/viber_image_2022-09-20_09-02-02-380.jpg\" /></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong>—The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente Bacarro, expressed his gratitude to the Bases Conversion and Development Authority (BCDA) for its invaluable contribution to the military’s modernization during a Forum on Monday, September 19, at the New Clark City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Chief of Staff said that the BCDA has contributed Php25.01-billion to the AFP Modernization Program from 2017 to 2022 alone.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/viber_image_2022-09-20_09-02-02-380.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-20T20:42:59+08:00","hits":231},{"id":1065,"title":"AFP welcomes new Secretary Joint Staff","slug":"afp-welcomes-new-secretary-joint-staff","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/SJS3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/SJS3.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) welcomed its new Secretary Joint Staff in a ceremony held on Friday, September 16.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Colonel Wilfredo B Manalang III PA(GSC) assumed his new position replacing Colonel Von Albert M Sumergido PA(GSC) during a Change of Chief of Office conducted at the Silid Lapu-Lapu, AFP General Headquarters Building.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/SJS3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-19T20:45:16+08:00","hits":1084},{"id":1066,"title":"PBBM to 6ID: \"Keep up the good work\"","slug":"pbbm-to-6id-keep-up-the-good-work","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/6ID5.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"603\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/6ID5.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP SIONGCO, Awang, DOS, Maguindanao— \"Keep up the good work.\" These are the words that are embedded in the speech of President and Commander-in-Chief of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, Ferdinand ‘Bong-Bong’ R. Marcos Jr., during his visit to Camp Siongco, Awang, DOS, Maguindanao on September 15, 2022.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Major General Roy M. Galido, Commander of Joint Task Force Central and 6ID, welcomed the President, along with Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro and Commander of Western Mindanao Command, Lt. Gen. Alfredo V. Rosario Jr., at the home of the Kampilan Troopers, where the country's highest official was also accorded with military honors upon his arrival at the 6ID Headquarters.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/6ID5.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-16T20:47:40+08:00","hits":309},{"id":1067,"title":"AFP to build 3-storey military hospital in Quezon Province","slug":"afp-to-build-3-storey-military-hospital-in-quezon-province","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/viber_image_2022-09-15_16-36-58-083.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"444\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/viber_image_2022-09-15_16-36-58-083.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines is set to improve health and medical services to its personnel with the construction of a three-storey hospital building.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro led the groundbreaking ceremony for the new building of Camp General Nakar Station Hospital on Wednesday, September 14, at the Headquarters of the Southern Luzon Command in Lucena, Quezon.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/viber_image_2022-09-15_16-36-58-083.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-15T20:49:45+08:00","hits":649},{"id":1080,"title":"PBBM leads AFP’s 87th-anniversary rites","slug":"pbbm-leads-afp-s-87th-anniversary-rites-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/PBBM leads AFPs 87th-anniversary rites.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The President and Commander in Chief His Excellency Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr leads the 87th founding anniversary rites of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) on Monday, December 19 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand here.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/PBBM%20leads%20AFPs%2087th-anniversary%20rites.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-13T05:36:21+08:00","hits":140},{"id":1079,"title":"Col Musñgi assumes as new JTF-NCR commander","slug":"col-musngi-assumes-as-new-jtf-ncr-commander-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Col Musgi assumes as new JTF-NCR commander.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Col Musgi assumes as new JTF-NCR commander.jpeg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines installed Colonel Alexei Musñgi as the new commander of Joint Task Force-National Capital Region (JTF-NCR). AFP Chief of Staff Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente Bacarro presided over the Change of Command Ceremony on Monday, October 24, at the AFP Commissioned Officers Club in Camp Aguinaldo.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Col%20Musgi%20assumes%20as%20new%20JTF-NCR%20commander.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-13T05:36:21+08:00","hits":115},{"id":1078,"title":"PBBM to 6ID: \"Keep up the good work\"","slug":"pbbm-to-6id-keep-up-the-good-work-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/PBBM to 6ID Keep up the good work.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"603\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/PBBM to 6ID Keep up the good work.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p>CAMP SIONGCO, Awang, DOS, Maguindanao— \"Keep up the good work.\" These are the words that are embedded in the speech of President and Commander-in-Chief of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, Ferdinand ‘Bong-Bong’ R. Marcos Jr., during his visit to Camp Siongco, Awang, DOS, Maguindanao on September 15, 2022.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/PBBM%20to%206ID%20Keep%20up%20the%20good%20work.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-13T05:36:21+08:00","hits":111},{"id":1077,"title":"AFP to build 3-storey military hospital in Quezon Province","slug":"afp-to-build-3-storey-military-hospital-in-quezon-province-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP to build 3-storey military hospital in Quezon Province.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"444\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/AFP to build 3-storey military hospital in Quezon Province.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines is set to improve health and medical services to its personnel with the construction of a three-storey hospital building.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP%20to%20build%203-storey%20military%20hospital%20in%20Quezon%20Province.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-13T05:36:21+08:00","hits":110},{"id":1076,"title":"AFP Expresses Gratitude to the Commander-in-Chief","slug":"afp-expresses-gratitude-to-the-commander-in-chief","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP Expresses Gratitude to the Commander-in-Chief.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/AFP Expresses Gratitude to the Commander-in-Chief.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p>Acting Vice Chief of Staff, AFP (VCSAFP) Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes had the opportunity to engage the President and Commander-in-Chief Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr. during the latter's visit to the shooting competition (BBM Cup 2022) held at MCS Firing Range in Barangay Suba, Paoay, Ilocos Norte on 08-11 Sep 2022.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP%20Expresses%20Gratitude%20to%20the%20Commander-in-Chief.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-13T05:36:21+08:00","hits":118},{"id":1075,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff leads Christening Ceremony for two Fast Attack Interdiction Crafts","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-leads-christening-ceremony-for-two-fast-attack-interdiction-crafts","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP Chief of Staff leads Christening Ceremony for two Fast Attack Interdiction Crafts.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/AFP Chief of Staff leads Christening Ceremony for two Fast Attack Interdiction Crafts.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p>Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro, the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), led the Christening Ceremony for the two Fast Attack Interdiction Crafts (FAIC) on September 6 at Roxas Boulevard, Manila.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP%20Chief%20of%20Staff%20leads%20Christening%20Ceremony%20for%20two%20Fast%20Attack%20Interdiction%20Crafts.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-13T05:36:21+08:00","hits":125},{"id":1074,"title":"STRENGTHENING ALLIANCE","slug":"strengthening-alliance","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/STRENGTHENING ALLIANCE.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/STRENGTHENING ALLIANCE.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">\r\n<p>Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes, The Deputy Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, met with Gen David H. Berger, Commandant of the US Marine Corps, during the latter’s courtesy call on 05 September 2022.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/STRENGTHENING%20ALLIANCE.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-13T05:36:21+08:00","hits":118},{"id":1073,"title":"Nurse Corps, AFP and Military Nurse Association of the Philippines Joint Anniversary Celebrations","slug":"nurse-corps-afp-and-military-nurse-association-of-the-philippines-joint-anniversary-celebrations","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Nurse Corps AFP and Military Nurse Association of the Philippines Joint Anniversary Celebrations.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/Nurse Corps AFP and Military Nurse Association of the Philippines Joint Anniversary Celebrations.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Chief of Staff Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP) Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro presided over the joint anniversary celebrations of the 84th Nurse Corps, AFP and 57th Military Nurse Association of the Philippines (MNAP) on Monday, August 5 at the Tejeros Hall, AFP Commissioned Officers Country in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/Nurse%20Corps%20AFP%20and%20Military%20Nurse%20Association%20of%20the%20Philippines%20Joint%20Anniversary%20Celebrations.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-13T05:36:21+08:00","hits":193},{"id":1072,"title":"BUILDING DIPLOMATIC RELATIONS","slug":"building-diplomatic-relations","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/BUILDING DIPLOMATIC RELATIONS.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/BUILDING DIPLOMATIC RELATIONS.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, met with HMA Laure Beafils, British Ambassador to the Philippines and Capt Graeme Davis, Non-Resident British Defense Attaché to the Philippines, during their courtesy call on 01 September 2022.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/BUILDING%20DIPLOMATIC%20RELATIONS.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-13T05:36:21+08:00","hits":124},{"id":1071,"title":"AFP renders final tribute to former president FVR as 30-day mourning ends","slug":"afp-renders-final-tribute-to-former-president-fvr-as-30-day-mourning-ends","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP renders final tribute to former president FVR as 30-day mourning ends.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"536\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/AFP renders final tribute to former president FVR as 30-day mourning ends.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines rendered its final tribute as it ended its 30-day mourning for the former president Fidel V Ramos on Monday, August 29, which started since the official reading of notice of death on July 31.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP%20renders%20final%20tribute%20to%20former%20president%20FVR%20as%2030-day%20mourning%20ends.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-13T05:36:21+08:00","hits":136},{"id":1070,"title":"AFP joins National Heroes Day Commemoration","slug":"afp-joins-national-heroes-day-commemoration","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP joins National Heroes Day Commemoration.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"496\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/AFP joins National Heroes Day Commemoration.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The Chief of Staff, AFP (CSAFP), Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro, visited the sailors and marines at the Philippine Navy Headquarters in Roxas Boulevard on Thursday, August 25.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP%20joins%20National%20Heroes%20Day%20Commemoration.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-13T05:36:21+08:00","hits":130},{"id":1069,"title":"UNIT VISIT","slug":"unit-visit-2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/UNIT VISIT.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/UNIT VISIT.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The Chief of Staff, AFP (CSAFP), Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro, visited the sailors and marines at the Philippine Navy Headquarters in Roxas Boulevard on Thursday, August 25.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/UNIT%20VISIT.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-13T05:36:21+08:00","hits":132},{"id":1068,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff joins Stormtroopers Day in Samar","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-joins-stormtroopers-day-in-samar","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> <img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP Chief of Staff joins Stormtroopers Day in Samar.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/AFP Chief of Staff joins Stormtroopers Day in Samar.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente Bacarro joined the 8th Infantry Division’s valiant Storm Troopers in celebrating their 34th founding anniversary in Catbalogan, Samar on Saturday, August 20.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/AFP%20Chief%20of%20Staff%20joins%20Stormtroopers%20Day%20in%20Samar.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-13T05:36:21+08:00","hits":136},{"id":1081,"title":"AFP Expresses Gratitude to the Commander-in-Chief","slug":"afp-expresses-gratitude-to-the-commander-in-chief-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/ALA5.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/ALA5.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Acting Vice Chief of Staff, AFP (VCSAFP) Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes had the opportunity to engage the President and Commander-in-Chief Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr. during the latter's visit to the shooting competition (BBM Cup 2022) held at MCS Firing Range in Barangay Suba, Paoay, Ilocos Norte on 08-11 Sep 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/ALA5.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-12T20:52:36+08:00","hits":204},{"id":1082,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff leads Christening Ceremony for two Fast Attack Interdiction Crafts","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-leads-christening-ceremony-for-two-fast-attack-interdiction-crafts-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/NAV2.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/NAV2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro, the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), led the Christening Ceremony for the two Fast Attack Interdiction Crafts (FAIC) on September 6 at Roxas Boulevard, Manila.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">These two missile-capable gunboats of the Philippine Navy, aptly named BRP Nestor Acero (PG901) and BRP Lolinato To-ong (PG902) in honor of two AFP Medal for Valor awardees, are part of the FAIC acquisition project under the Revised AFP Modernization Program-Horizon 2. A total of eight units were ordered worth Php10 billion.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/NAV2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-07T20:54:10+08:00","hits":222},{"id":1083,"title":"Nurse Corps, AFP and  Military Nurse Association of the Philippines Joint Anniversary Celebrations","slug":"nurse-corps-afp-and-military-nurse-association-of-the-philippines-joint-anniversary-celebrations-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/NAR7.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/NAR7.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Chief of Staff Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP) Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro presided over the joint anniversary celebrations of the 84th Nurse Corps, AFP and 57th Military Nurse Association of the Philippines (MNAP) on Monday, August 5 at the Tejeros Hall, AFP Commissioned Officers Country in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/NAR7.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-06T21:00:44+08:00","hits":1213},{"id":1084,"title":"STRENGTHENING ALLIANCE ","slug":"strengthening-alliance-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/TTT5.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/TTT5.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes, The Deputy Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, met with Gen David H. Berger, Commandant of the US Marine Corps, during the latter’s courtesy call on 05 September 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/TTT5.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-06T20:56:10+08:00","hits":321},{"id":1085,"title":"BUILDING DIPLOMATIC RELATIONS","slug":"building-diplomatic-relations-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"m8h3af8h l7ghb35v kjdc1dyq kmwttqpk gh25dzvf n3t5jt4f\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/301861660_435339668628449_4868390925163293998_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/301861660_435339668628449_4868390925163293998_n.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, met with HMA Laure Beafils, British Ambassador to the Philippines and Capt Graeme Davis, Non-Resident British Defense Attaché to the Philippines, during their courtesy call on 01 September 2022.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l7ghb35v kjdc1dyq kmwttqpk gh25dzvf jikcssrz n3t5jt4f\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Both sides expressed the importance of developing cooperation and discussed regional dynamics and bilateral opportunities between the Philippines and the United Kingdom.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/301861660_435339668628449_4868390925163293998_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-09-05T21:02:50+08:00","hits":257},{"id":1086,"title":"AFP renders final tribute to former president FVR as 30-day mourning ends+","slug":"afp-renders-final-tribute-to-former-president-fvr-as-30-day-mourning-ends-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September 2023/FVR2.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"536\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/September 2023/FVR2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines rendered its final tribute as it ended its 30-day mourning for the former president Fidel V Ramos on Monday, August 29, which started since the official reading of notice of death on July 31.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente O. Bacarro led the ceremony at the AFP General Headquarters, which was simultaneously held at the headquarters of the Major Services, Unified Commands, and the Philippine Military Academy.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/September%202023/FVR2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-30T21:08:31+08:00","hits":183},{"id":1087,"title":"AFP joins National Heroes Day Commemoration","slug":"afp-joins-national-heroes-day-commemoration-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/viber_image_2022-08-29_12-29-22-039 1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"496\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/viber_image_2022-08-29_12-29-22-039 1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AFP Chief of Staff Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro joins the President and Commander-in-Chief Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr. and the entire nation in commemorating the National Heroes Day at the Libingan ng Mga Bayani in Taguig City, today August 29.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/viber_image_2022-08-29_12-29-22-039%201.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-30T07:58:18+08:00","hits":235},{"id":1088,"title":"UNIT VISIT ","slug":"unit-visit-2-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/PH7.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/PH7.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Chief of Staff, AFP (CSAFP), Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro, visited the sailors and marines at the Philippine Navy Headquarters in Roxas Boulevard on Thursday, August 25.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In his talk to troops, the CSAFP reiterated the Commander-in-Chief's emphasis on safeguarding the country's sovereignty and territorial integrity.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/PH7.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-26T08:01:36+08:00","hits":239},{"id":1089,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff joins Stormtroopers Day in Samar","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-joins-stormtroopers-day-in-samar-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"l7ghb35v kjdc1dyq kmwttqpk gh25dzvf jikcssrz n3t5jt4f\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/SAM3.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/SAM3.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente Bacarro joined the 8th Infantry Division’s valiant Storm Troopers in celebrating their 34th founding anniversary in Catbalogan, Samar on Saturday, August 20.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l7ghb35v kjdc1dyq kmwttqpk gh25dzvf jikcssrz n3t5jt4f\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The anniversary marked the Division’s more than three decades of successful internal security operations to dismantle and destroy the remaining guerrilla fronts of the communist terrorist groups in the area.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l7ghb35v kjdc1dyq kmwttqpk gh25dzvf jikcssrz n3t5jt4f\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The occasion was highlighted by the wreath-laying ceremony at 8ID Headquarters to honor the brave Stormtroopers who paid the ultimate sacrifice in the performance of their duty.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/SAM3.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-22T08:13:35+08:00","hits":300},{"id":1090,"title":"MGen Sequitin bows out of military service, Col Aguilar takes command of CRSAFP","slug":"mgen-sequitin-bows-out-of-military-service-col-aguilar-takes-command-of-crsafp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"l7ghb35v kjdc1dyq kmwttqpk gh25dzvf jikcssrz n3t5jt4f\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/CRSAFP.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"586\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/CRSAFP.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - The Commander of the Civil Relations Service, Armed Forces of the Philippines, Maj. Gen. Manuel V Sequitin bowed out of service in a Change of Command and Retirement Ceremony at AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo on Thursday, August 18, after over 37 years of outstanding military service.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l7ghb35v kjdc1dyq kmwttqpk gh25dzvf jikcssrz n3t5jt4f\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">He was replaced in an acting capacity by Col Medel M Aguilar in the ceremony presided by the Chief of Staff AFP Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/CRSAFP.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-22T08:11:09+08:00","hits":885},{"id":1091,"title":"REGIONAL PARTNERS","slug":"regional-partners","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"m8h3af8h l7ghb35v kjdc1dyq kmwttqpk gh25dzvf n3t5jt4f\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/rp.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"595\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/rp.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente Bacarro, receives Lt. Gen. Greg Bilton, the Chief of Joint Operations, Australian Defense Force, during his visit and courtesy call at the General Headquarters in Quezon City today, August 18.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l7ghb35v kjdc1dyq kmwttqpk gh25dzvf jikcssrz n3t5jt4f\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">In their meeting, the CSAFP expressed his appreciation to Lt. Gen. Bilton for Australia’s continued support to the AFP. The two military leaders also discussed further strengthening cooperation on maritime domain awareness capabilities and the possibility of future joint integration training to enhance interoperability between the two armed forces. (Photo by A2C Ted Castro PAF/PAO, AFP)</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/rp.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-22T08:07:29+08:00","hits":268},{"id":1092,"title":"STRENGTHENING PARTNERSHIP","slug":"strengthening-partnership","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"m8h3af8h l7ghb35v kjdc1dyq kmwttqpk gh25dzvf n3t5jt4f\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/SA.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/SA.jpg\" /></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), Lt. Gen. Bartolome Vicente Bacarro, meets with the Commander of the United States Pacific Fleet, Admiral Samuel Paparo, on Thursday, August 18.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"l7ghb35v kjdc1dyq kmwttqpk gh25dzvf jikcssrz n3t5jt4f\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">Admiral Paparo’s visit follows the recently concluded Pacific Partnership 2022 and the Rim of the Pacific exercises. In their meeting, the two military leaders affirmed their desire for greater cooperation, especially in establishing real-time information sharing and collaboration in maritime domain awareness. They also anticipate the successful conduct of marquee activities, including Exercise Sama-Sama between the Philippine Fleet and the US Navy in October, the Exercise Kamandag between the Philippine and US Marine Corps in October, and the Balikatan Exercises next year. </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photo by A2CCastro PAF/ PAOAFP)</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/SA.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-22T08:04:43+08:00","hits":217},{"id":1093,"title":"Korea Air Force’s 53rd Air Demonstration Group in Basa Air Base","slug":"korea-air-force-s-53rd-air-demonstration-group-in-basa-air-base","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/PHR6.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"554\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/PHR6.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro attended the Aerobatic Show performed by Republic of Korea Air Force’s 53rd Air Demonstration Group in Basa Air Base, Floridablanca, Pampanga on Monday, August 15.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Department of National Defense Office-in-Charge, Senior Undersecretary Jose Faustino Jr was the Guest of Honor during the event which sought to highlight the strong relations between the Philippines and South Korea.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Demonstration Group also known as the ‘Black Eagles’ utilized eight T-50Bs for their air maneuvers. This is the last leg of their tour before heading back to South Korea. (Photos by A2C Ted Castro PAF/PAOAFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/PHR6.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-15T08:16:44+08:00","hits":234},{"id":1094,"title":"AFP joins National IHL Day Commemoration","slug":"afp-joins-national-ihl-day-commemoration","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" style=\"text-align: justify;\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\"><strong><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/viber_image_2022-08-12_15-01-32-439.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/viber_image_2022-08-12_15-01-32-439.jpg\" /></strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" style=\"text-align: justify;\" data-offset-key=\"bvfpf-0-0\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong> – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined various government and non-government agencies in the national commemoration of the International Humanitarian Law (IHL) Day on Friday, August 12.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"bc5kt-0-0\"> </span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify;\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"bksft\" data-offset-key=\"bmgbi-0-0\">\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bmgbi-0-0\"><span data-offset-key=\"bmgbi-0-0\">The IHL day commemoration ceremony was held at the AFP Commissioned Officers Country in Camp Aguinaldo, with the Department of National Defense (DND) serving as the host. One of the event’s highlights was the opening of a photo exhibit showcasing the importance of IHL and Human Rights.</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"bmgbi-0-0\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/viber_image_2022-08-12_15-01-32-439.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-12T00:18:30+08:00","hits":382},{"id":1095,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff meets with the Chief of Staff of the United States Air Force","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-meets-with-the-chief-of-staff-of-the-united-states-air-force","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/US1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/US1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro met with the Chief of Staff of the United States Air Force, General Charles Q Brown Jr, on Wednesday, August 10, during the latter's courtesy call held at the General Headquarters Building in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The two leaders discussed efforts to further strengthen cooperation that would benefit the Air Forces of the Philippines and United States. (Photos by Donald Viluan/PAO)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/US1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-11T08:26:29+08:00","hits":201},{"id":1096,"title":"AFP renders full military honors to FVR","slug":"afp-renders-full-military-honors-to-fvr","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/0-02-06-46719eb01c5dd69652fc0ed6df2221ac923717cfd5aa074a1245d82acb81acbb_6f579dba369d10de.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/0-02-06-46719eb01c5dd69652fc0ed6df2221ac923717cfd5aa074a1245d82acb81acbb_6f579dba369d10de.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines rendered full military honors on Tuesday, August 9, to former president Fidel V Ramos during the state funeral for the 12th President of the Republic of the Philippines.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A battalion-sized contingent of honor guards tendered departure honors for the late president at Heritage Park where he was laid in state.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/0-02-06-46719eb01c5dd69652fc0ed6df2221ac923717cfd5aa074a1245d82acb81acbb_6f579dba369d10de.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-09T10:20:29+08:00","hits":617},{"id":1097,"title":"LtGen Bacarro assumes as new Chief of Staff, AFP","slug":"ltgen-bacarro-assumes-as-new-chief-of-staff-afp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/0-02-06-ccef98642a578a5cd3298cb761e88f2571ce6610515ba03d6a9c3c9941dd827f_62cd5862e61c7275.jpg\" width=\"640\" height=\"960\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/0-02-06-ccef98642a578a5cd3298cb761e88f2571ce6610515ba03d6a9c3c9941dd827f_62cd5862e61c7275.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - Lieutenant General Bartolome Vicente O Bacarro assumed as the new Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, replacing General Andres C Centino on Monday, August 8, in a Change of Command Ceremony presided by President Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A member of the Philippine Military Academy Maringal Class of 1988, Lt. Gen. Bacarro held command and staff positions that prepared him for his present designation. He is the current commander of Southern Luzon Command (SOLCOM), which covers CALABARZON, MIMAROPA, and Bicol regions. Prior to his stint as SOLCOM Commander, he was the commander of the 2nd Infantry Division, Philippine Army, and Commander of the 502nd Infantry Brigade.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/0-02-06-ccef98642a578a5cd3298cb761e88f2571ce6610515ba03d6a9c3c9941dd827f_62cd5862e61c7275.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-08T10:23:06+08:00","hits":678},{"id":1098,"title":"Philippine Soldier-Athletes dominate 2022 World Eskrima Kali Arnis Championship","slug":"philippine-soldier-athletes-dominate-2022-world-eskrima-kali-arnis-championship","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><strong><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/viber_image_2022-08-03_10-00-01-058.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/viber_image_2022-08-03_10-00-01-058.jpg\" /></strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City -</strong> Arnisadors and Eskrimadors from the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) dominated the recently concluded 16th World Eskrima Kali Aris Federation (WEKAF) Championship held in Mandaue City, Cebu from 17-22 July 2022, defeating participants from eight countries.</p>\r\n<p>The AFP sent nine soldier-athletes who contributed 13 gold, eight silver and three bronze medals to the overall medal standing.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/viber_image_2022-08-03_10-00-01-058.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-03T10:30:13+08:00","hits":373},{"id":1099,"title":"AFP reaffirms commitment to IHL","slug":"afp-reaffirms-commitment-to-ihl","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/IHL5.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/IHL5.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines opened on Monday, August 1, its month-long commemoration of the International Humanitarian Law (IHL) with an oath-taking ceremony at the General Headquarters in Quezon City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Brig. Gen. Joel Alejandro S Nacnac, Director of the AFP Center for Law of Armed Conflict, led the reading of the pledge that reaffirms the AFP’s adherence to the principles of IHL and commitment to its promulgation to all military and civilian personnel.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/IHL5.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-01T10:35:32+08:00","hits":393},{"id":1100,"title":"AFP flies the Philippine flag at half-staff","slug":"afp-flies-the-philippine-flag-at-half-staff","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August 2023/FVR5.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/August 2023/FVR5.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines flies the Philippine flag at half-staff in mourning of former President Fidel V Ramos during the flag-raising ceremony at Camp Aguinaldo in Quezon City on Monday, August 1. AFP officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian human resources wore black bands to commiserate with the passing of the former Commander-in-Chief.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/August%202023/FVR5.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-08-01T10:32:54+08:00","hits":374},{"id":1101,"title":"AFP Statement on the passing of Former President Fidel V. Ramos","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-passing-of-former-president-fidel-v-ramos","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"800\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines mourns the passing of the 12th President of the Republic of the Philippines, Fidel V. Ramos, who died on Sunday, July 31.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/256439877_250686227093795_5893832530141949744_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-31T10:45:54+08:00","hits":294},{"id":1102,"title":"Relief Operations","slug":"relief-operations","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/RO2.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/RO2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) utilized its personnel and aircraft assets in distributing relief goods to the seven (7) isolated municipalities of Abra (Boliney, Bucloc, Daguioman, Luba, Tubo, Malibcong, and Lacub) due to the 7.3 magnitude earthquake last July 27.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/RO2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-29T10:49:43+08:00","hits":273},{"id":1103,"title":"AFP deploys 14 SRR teams in quake-hit areas","slug":"afp-deploys-14-srr-teams-in-quake-hit-areas","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/abr2.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"361\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/abr2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines deployed 14 search, rescue, and retrieval teams (SRR) to areas affected by the 7.3-magnitude earthquake that hit Northern Luzon yesterday, July 27.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Since yesterday, the 24th Infantry Battalion (24IB) has helped evacuate the patients in a hospital in Bangued, Abra. 71IB deployed personnel to rescue affected residents in Vigan, Ilocos Sur. 54IB, 72nd Division Reconnaissance Company, 502nd Infantry Brigade, and CAFGU Active Auxillary units helped in road clearing, provided transportation assistance, and conducted search and rescue operations in different areas in Northern Luzon.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/abr2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-28T10:54:52+08:00","hits":351},{"id":1104,"title":"Army reservists, ROTC assist DSWD in relief effort","slug":"army-reservists-rotc-assist-dswd-in-relief-effort","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/ROTC2.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/ROTC2.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - Philippine Army Reservists and ROTC cadets from the 14th Regional Community Defense Group, assist the DSWD in hauling relief items for victims of the 7.3-magnitude earthquake that hit Northern Luzon on July 27, 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/ROTC2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-28T10:52:56+08:00","hits":222},{"id":1105,"title":"PH-US conclude PH-US Executive Committee Meeting, Remain Firm Allies","slug":"ph-us-conclude-ph-us-executive-committee-meeting-remain-firm-allies","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><b><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/viber_image_2022-07-21_09-05-48-633.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/viber_image_2022-07-21_09-05-48-633.jpg\" /></b></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><b>MANILA, Philippines. </b></strong>MGen Jeffrey Hechanova PAF, J5, AFP and BGen Jennifer M Short, Deputy Director Strategic Planning and Policy, J5 USINDOPACOM led the Philippine and US delegation, respectively during the  Philippines-United States Mutual-Defense Board – Security Engagement Board (MDB-SEB) Executive Committee (EXECOM) Meeting  held on 12-13 July 2022 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/viber_image_2022-07-21_09-05-48-633.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-21T11:08:57+08:00","hits":320},{"id":1106,"title":"Philippines, Japan and US hold Trilateral Security Talks","slug":"philippines-japan-and-us-hold-trilateral-security-talks","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><b><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/TJST_2.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/TJST_2.jpg\" /></b></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><b>MANILA, Philippines.</b></strong> Defense Forces Planners from the Armed Forces of the Philippines, MGen Jeffrey Hechanova, Japan Self-Defense Forces RAdm Hiroshi Egawa and United States Indo-Pacific Command BGen Jennifer Short met last July 13 for the Trilateral Joint Staff Talks (TJST). Said engagement aims to strengthen the trilateral security partnerships of the Philippines, Japan and the US.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/TJST_2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-21T11:07:00+08:00","hits":250},{"id":1107,"title":"Philippines, Japan agree to deepen Security Partnerships","slug":"philippines-japan-agree-to-deepen-security-partnerships","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><b><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/MCWG_1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/MCWG_1.jpg\" /></b></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong><b>Manila, Philippines.</b></strong> The Deputy Chief of Staff for Plans, Armed Forces of the Philippines, MGen Jeffrey C. Hechanova and Director-General, Defense Plans and Policy Department, Japan Self-Defense Forces, RAdm Hiroshi Egawa held the 3<sup>rd</sup> AFP-JSDF Military Cooperation Working Group Staff Talks on July 14-15, 2022.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/MCWG_1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-21T10:59:24+08:00","hits":277},{"id":1108,"title":"Philippine Navy's BRP Antonio Luna tests firepower during RIMPAC live-fire exercise","slug":"philippine-navys-brp-antonio-luna-tests-firepower-during-rimpac-live-fire-exercise","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/80327169-06A2-4B42-A42D-9ECDAA46F0B7.jpeg\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/80327169-06A2-4B42-A42D-9ECDAA46F0B7.jpeg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Philippine Navy tested the BRP Antonio Luna's (FF151) anti-submarine and main battery capabilities in the Rim of the Pacific (RIMPAC) exercise held in Hawaii from July 12 to 16.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/80327169-06A2-4B42-A42D-9ECDAA46F0B7.jpeg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-20T11:11:54+08:00","hits":195},{"id":1109,"title":"LtGen Centino Convenes first Command Conference as AFP Chief","slug":"ltgen-centino-convenes-first-command-conference-as-afp-chief","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Article 5.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Article 5.jpg\" /></strong></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, QUEZON CITY -</strong> The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) held a Command Conference on Saturday Nov 13, 2021, a day after the new Chief of Staff, Lieutenant General Andres Centino assumed his post.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">LtGen Centino met with the top AFP commanders and principal staff officers at the AFP Commissioned Officers’ Country at Camp Aguinaldo to deliver his initial marching orders.<span class=\"mce-nbsp-wrap\" contenteditable=\"false\"> </span><span class=\"mce-nbsp-wrap\" contenteditable=\"false\"> </span></span></p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Article%205.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-18T08:58:21+08:00","hits":160},{"id":1110,"title":"Courtesy Call of Brig. Gen. Jennifer M Short USAF","slug":"courtesy-call-of-brig-gen-jennifer-m-short-usaf","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/SHORT4.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"520\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/SHORT4.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Brig. Gen. Jennifer M Short USAF, the Deputy Director for Strategic Planning and Policy Directorate of the United States Indo-Pacific Command renders a courtesy call to Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes, The Deputy Chief of Staff Armed Forces of the Philippines (TDCSAFP) at the General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City on Tuesday, 12 July 2022.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Brig. Gen. Short attended the Phil-US Executive Committee Meeting as part of the Mutual Defense Board-Security Engagement Board (MDB-SEB) planning cycle./// (Photo by:  SN1 Donald Viluan PN (Ret)/PAO AFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/SHORT4.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-14T11:17:32+08:00","hits":272},{"id":1111,"title":"Courtesy Call of Rear Admiral Hiroshi Egawa","slug":"courtesy-call-of-rear-admiral-hiroshi-egawa","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july 2023/EGA1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/july 2023/EGA1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Rear Admiral Hiroshi Egawa of the Defense Plans and Policy Department, Japan Self-Defense Forces (JSDF), renders a courtesy call to Vice Admiral Rommel Anthony SD Reyes, The Deputy Chief of Staff Armed Forces of the Philippines (TDCSAFP)at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City on Wednesday, 13 July 2022.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">RAdm Egawa is in the country for the AFP-JSDF Military Cooperation Working Group Staff Talks from 14 - 15 July 2022.///<br /><br />(Photo by: SN1 Donald Viluan PN (Ret)/PAO AFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/july%202023/EGA1.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-14T11:15:24+08:00","hits":220},{"id":1115,"title":"General Faustino Jr relinquishes Chief of Staff post to Lt. Gen. Centino","slug":"general-faustino-jr-relinquishes-chief-of-staff-v2","category":1,"category_name":"Uncategorised","category_slug":"uncategorised","intro_html":"<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Feat Article 1.jpg\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Feat Article 1.jpg\" /></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong> — General Jose Faustino Jr relinquished his post as Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) in a Joint Change of Command and Retirement Ceremony today, November 12 as he bowed out of service after over 37 years in the military.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Lt. Gen. Andres Centino, the current Commanding General of the Philippine Army, took the helm as the 57th Chief of Staff of the AFP.</span></p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Feat%20Article%201.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2022-07-13T02:02:14+08:00","hits":192}]}